# Complexity

### Time Complexity

Binary search takes:

```text
O(log N)
```

for each test case.

### Space Complexity

```text
O(1)
```

No additional data structure is required.

---

# Why Binary Search?

A linear search would find the minimum in:

```text
O(N)
```

But because the array is a **rotated sorted array**, we can use its structure to eliminate half of the search space at every step.

Therefore:

```text
Linear Search  → O(N)
Binary Search  → O(log N)
```

---

# Key Takeaway

For a sorted array rotated to the right:

> **The number of rotations is exactly the index of the minimum element.**

Because the array is rotated and sorted, the minimum can be found efficiently using **Binary Search**.

### Pattern

```text
Rotated Sorted Array
        ↓
Find Minimum
        ↓
Index of Minimum
        ↓
Number of Rotations
```
